  "coverage": [
    "Ordinary missile direct contact remains immediate. No area hurt at blast ages 0..8; radius2/source100 at9, radius6/source50 at10..11, no damage from12, removal20. MC base damage retains direct2.4, inner4, outer2 before native target scaling, armor and immunity.",
    "The two area rings share contact-before-hurt UUID history. Clearing native hurt immunity every tick in the isolated area test does not cause repeated area damage. Actual reloads at ages8 and9 preserve weapon profile, clock and contact history; late outer-ring entry remains eligible.",
    "Native wall occlusion, actual tank surface/armor, seated living-entity protection, friendly hull protection, missing owner and stale saved timeline are exercised. Version1 Hellfire saves still load; malformed or ambiguous new profile saves fail closed.",
    "Normal real-player payload handling fires downward from altitude8 at ground infantry and a ground tank. Direct health loss occurs before age9, remains stable until the delayed phase, then additional damage is accepted. No artificial hurt-immunity clearing is used in these ground-attack scenes.",
    "Both normal integrated client input/network paths alternate real pod launches at5-tick cadence, consume finite stocks, switch back to one Hellfire, hide exactly one spent Hellfire rail and synchronize HUD. Each rapid impact creates one server timeline and one cosmetic receipt, both expire before scene completion.",
    "Native client SoundManager reports active rocket, impact, rotor and turbine sounds with physical OpenAL gain0 and logical sound settings1. This establishes native playback, not human listening or source waveform identity."
  ],
  "failuresAndFixtureChanges": [
    "Initial wall fixture overlapped the blocked target body with its wall and observed unrelated damage. The target now stands clear at z4 and asserts native noCollision; production occlusion/damage was not weakened.",
    "One old Neo friendly-near-enemy test failed its fixed-world-tick hover/gun assertion; the next diagnostic run passed. The exact original failing state was not captured. The fixture now requires an observed real FIRE opportunity and at least40 entity ticks through recovery, retaining gun>3, zero rockets and unchanged ally health. This also strengthens the old hover-only evidence. Both final native suites use this revised fixture.",
    "A diagnostic-only compile error (save() instead of save(CompoundTag)) was corrected before the diagnostic native rerun; no production change was involved."
  ],
  "review": {
    "method": "Both native framebuffer16-frame contact sheets and one full-size active-burst frame per platform visually inspected. HUD, finite ammunition, small trail/impact smoke and normal expiry are visible; authored visual presentation is not an original-FX fidelity approval."
  },
  "limits": [
    "20Hz quantization is an explicit Minecraft adaptation of source .433333/.466667/.566667/1 second track boundaries. Source scheduler/contact behavior is from hashed static disassembly; the original executable/frame-order was not run.",
    "Source direct60 and area100/50 ratios are preserved at MC balance scale, while Minecraft hurt immunity and event cancellation remain authoritative. The directly hit infantry loses20 total rather than the naive direct12+inner20=32 sum; no immunity bypass was added.",
    "Immediate MC radius4 permission-controlled block damage remains a separate adaptation. Source WorldDamage transform, impulses, friendly-fire factors and CollideWith48 are not fully ported.",
    "AI70mm entry, complete original weighted maneuver bank, player accuracy/dead reckoning/upgrades, exact source model/FX/audio identity and dedicated multiplayer validation remain open.",
    "The vehicle ammunition key remains user-configurable and unbound by default. Client harness queues the same internal switch request; this does not test an OS key assignment.",
    "No release, install, commit, user-world change or new destruction-visual rerun is claimed. Earlier vehicle destruction evidence remains historical."
